Nothing is vendored. What was taken is two small designs, each re-implemented
against this project's own shapes, and each borrow site names its original in a
comment:

  agent/worker.py    the task table's shape and its transitions, from
                     cron/executions.py:139-200. Two ideas: a status transition
                     written as UPDATE ... WHERE status='queued' with rowcount
                     checked, so it applies exactly once and a second attempt
                     declines; and liveness by pid AND process start time,
                     because pids are recycled and the pair is not. This
                     project's version REQUEUES an abandoned task where Hermes
                     marks it unknown and refuses to retry - it checkpoints
                     after every node, so resuming cannot re-fire a tool.

  agent/context.py   _clean_boundary() / _snap()
                     Compaction boundary handling, from
                     trajectory_compressor.py:524-560. A boundary must not land
                     between a tool call and the result that answers it; the
                     search moves forward to the nearest clean turn and falls
                     back to moving backward. This project's version inspects
                     content BLOCK TYPES rather than Hermes's `from == "tool"`
                     turn marker, because its messages carry Anthropic-shaped
                     content lists rather than a role string.

